---
description: Design handoff rules for the Block Date Range feature (KIS Creativity Space)
alwaysApply: false
---

When implementing the Block Date Range feature:

- The spec is handoff_cursor_block_date_range/README.md — labels, validation copy, and the applicability rule are exact.
- designs/*.dc.html are HTML prototypes for behavior reference only. Never copy their markup, the DCLogic classes, or support.js.
- start applies to weekly blocks only; once blocks keep their single DATE. Missing start = no lower bound (legacy behavior, no migration).
- Enforce the [start, until] window in EVERY consumer and server-side — Schedule, Book training, and the creation-time conflict check must all use the same rule.
- ENDS < STARTS blocks saving with the inline error; never silently swap the dates.
- The list when-label shows FROM/UNTIL segments only when the corresponding date is stored.
